\title{Free Time Slots}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Problem}

Given booked time slots like [[09:00-10:30]], one per line on standard
input, we print the free slots within the working day 08:00--17:00 in the
same format. Bookings may overlap, touch, and come in any order.

\section{Approach}

We work in minutes since midnight. The algorithm is:
\begin{enumerate}
\item parse each booking into a pair [[(start, end)]],
\item sort by start,
\item sweep through, keeping a cursor [[pos]] of the end of everything
      seen so far (initially the start of the day); whenever a booking
      starts after the cursor, the gap is a free slot,
\item finally, if the cursor is before the end of the day, the remainder
      is free.
\end{enumerate}
Bookings are clipped implicitly: the cursor never moves before the day
start, and gaps are limited to the day end. Empty gaps (touching
bookings) are never emitted.

